WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.243
The clock makes it real. Huddle enters the
draft room, with recommendations

00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:07.550
on one side and Yahoo on the other.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:15.265
Josh Allen. Then Chase Brown. Recommended by
Huddle, selected through

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:17.927
computer use, and confirmed in Yahoo.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:25.955
Terry McLaurin joins the roster.
Reconciliation checks the accepted pick, so

00:00:25.955 --> 00:00:27.964
the board can move forward.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.476
Sometimes the call changes. Bucky Irving was
available in Yahoo but missing

00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:38.444
from Huddle. The assistant made an audible.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:45.250
This first live run exposed interruptions,
missing player details, and one

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.928
missed deadline. Those failures belong in
the evidence.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.716
Twenty roster spots filled. All one hundred
twenty results reconciled. A real

00:00:55.716 --> 00:00:59.655
draft, an honest review. Huddle. Your
league. Your call.
